\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Three-regime fragmentation framework from 208 Athena++ simulations. Color shows density contrast $C$. Three regimes: Magnetically subcritical (red, $\beta \leq 0.15$): minimal fragmentation; Magnetically regulated (yellow/orange, $0.2 \leq \beta \leq 2$): intermediate fragmentation; Thermally dominated (blue, $\beta \geq 3$): vigorous fragmentation. Typical HGBS filament conditions fall in the magnetically regulated regime.}}{12}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:regime}{{6}{12}{Three-regime fragmentation framework from 208 Athena++ simulations. Color shows density contrast $C$. Three regimes: Magnetically subcritical (red, $\beta \leq 0.15$): minimal fragmentation; Magnetically regulated (yellow/orange, $0.2 \leq \beta \leq 2$): intermediate fragmentation; Thermally dominated (blue, $\beta \geq 3$): vigorous fragmentation. Typical HGBS filament conditions fall in the magnetically regulated regime}{figure.6}{}}
