\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {10}{\ignorespaces Cross-campaign $\lambda /W$ comparison. Longitudinal-field filaments (blue) show strong $\beta $-dependence: $\lambda /W$ decreases from $\sim 4.7$ at $\beta = 0.3$ to $\sim 2.8$ at $\beta = 2.0$. Perpendicular-field filaments (red) show $\lambda /W \approx 1.25$ ($\beta \geq 1.0$) or FLAT profiles ($\beta \leq 0.5$). Horizontal dashed line shows HGBS observational result ($\lambda /W = 2.84 \pm 0.12$).}}{18}{figure.10}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:cross_campaign_lambdaW}{{10}{18}{Cross-campaign $\lambda /W$ comparison. Longitudinal-field filaments (blue) show strong $\beta $-dependence: $\lambda /W$ decreases from $\sim 4.7$ at $\beta = 0.3$ to $\sim 2.8$ at $\beta = 2.0$. Perpendicular-field filaments (red) show $\lambda /W \approx 1.25$ ($\beta \geq 1.0$) or FLAT profiles ($\beta \leq 0.5$). Horizontal dashed line shows HGBS observational result ($\lambda /W = 2.84 \pm 0.12$)}{figure.10}{}}
